{#
   THE ADMIN LIST PAGE — one page shape for every admin list.

   `_catalogue.html.twig` did this for the public side and `_data_table.html.twig`
   did it for the table itself. This is the layer between them: the page *around*
   the table, which was still being written out by hand fifteen times.

   ⚠️ **What was actually wrong.** There were two skeletons in the codebase and
   nothing said which was current. Eleven pages used `admin-page` + `admin-layout`;
   five used `main-content` + `admin-main` + `admin-content-grid` +
   `admin-main-content` — four nested wrappers to do the job of one. Same job,
   same sidebar, different DOM, so they could never be restyled together.

   ⚠️ **The flashes were the tell.** This shell renders them; before it, one page
   styled its own success flash with a `style=""` attribute carrying a hardcoded
   green. A page that has to remember to draw its own confirmation message is a
   page that will one day forget.

   ─── S134h/S140/S141 — the settled format ──────────────────────────────────

   Four rounds in `/admin/design#filtres` decided where each kind of control
   lives (S134h); S140 took the seams out; S141 made it the only format there
   is. **One card, four bands, separated by a 1 px rule and a ground — never by
   a gap:**

     band     the **menu name** as the title, the count beneath it, the search,
              and **one green named button** for what the page creates. Never an
              icon alone: green makes it findable, the words say what it makes.
     filters  `_admin_filters.html.twig` — one tile row for the facet that
              defines the page, then "Affiner" dropdowns with **location
              first**, the whole group gone on a single-location install.
     message  the flash, when there is one.
     rows     the table.

   Measured on `/admin/machines` at 1440 px: **267 px** from the top of the band
   to the first row, against 430 px for the three floating cards it replaced,
   and 394 px for the hand-written headers before those.

   ⚠️ **The title is the name of the menu entry, not a sentence written for the
   page** (operator, 2026-08-16). The caller does not pass one: the shell reads
   it from `NavBuilder` via `nav_admin_title()`, which is why the per-page
   `*.title` keys could be deleted from all five catalogues instead of
   maintained. `page_title` remains as an override for the three screens the
   menu cannot name: an event's registrations, a package being edited, and the
   staff pass desk, which is not an admin destination at all.

   ⚠️ **There is no `description`.** The band's subtitle is the count and only
   the count. Every screen here that has nothing to count already explains
   itself in its own body, so the per-page description keys went the same way as
   the titles.

   Use it with `{% embed %}`:

     {% embed 'site/_admin_list.html.twig' with {
         action_label: 'admin_places.list_action'|trans,
         action_route: 'app_admin_place_new',
         panel_title: 'admin_places.list_panel'|trans,
     } %}
         {% block content %}…the table…{% endblock %}
     {% endembed %}

   Parameters, all optional:

     page_title     overrides the menu name, for a screen the menu cannot name.
                    ⚠️ Named `page_title` and not `title`: an `{% embed %}`
                    without `only` merges the parent context, so a controller
                    that happens to pass a `title` variable — `/admin/machines/
                    categories` does — would silently become the page heading.
     action_label   the green button's words. Omitted = no button.
     action_route   where it goes
     action_params  route parameters, if it needs any
     panel_title    the accessible heading of the section holding the table
     panel_note     the count line, in the caller's own words ("11 machine(s)")
                    — the noun changes per list, so the shell cannot write it
     list_count     rows currently shown
     list_total     rows before any filter. When it is larger than `list_count`
                    the shell replaces `panel_note` with "3 sur 11" — otherwise
                    the search box reads as if it only looked at this page.

   Filter panel (handed straight to `_admin_filters.html.twig`):

     list_route, list_route_params, list_query
     list_tiles, list_tiles_label, list_tiles_preserve_query
     list_refine    the "Affiner" dropdowns
     venue_context  becomes the first of them
     list_client_filter  filter in the browser instead of navigating

   Search:

     list_search_placeholder  set it and the search box appears in the band.
                              Unset = no search, and the band shows nothing
                              between the title and the button.
     list_search              its current value

   Blocks:

     header_extra an extra control on the band, after the green button
                  (`/admin/rfid-readers`' pairing dialog, `/admin/reporting`'s
                  export link)
     filters      an escape hatch for a page whose controls genuinely are not
                  facets (`/admin/reporting`'s date range). Needs `has_filters`;
                  renders as a band of its own under the filter band.
     content      the table — normally an `{% embed %}` of `_data_table`
     panel_extra  anything after the table, inside the card
     after        anything after the card entirely

   ⚠️ This template computes NOTHING and knows what none of these things are.
   Same rule as `_catalogue`: an `{% if %}` on entity type here and it has
   stopped being a shell.
#}
{% include 'site/_header.html.twig' %}

{# ⚠️ **S141 — there is one format now, and no parameter selects it.** Three
   shapes lived in this file at once: the full-bleed slab of the hand-written
   headers, `hero: 'compact'` (S136, the mockup's rounded strip) and
   `hero: 'merged'` (S140, the single card). The operator validated the merged
   card on `/admin/machines` on 2026-08-16 after four rounds, so the flag, the
   two other shapes and the `.is-merged` variant class are gone: what is left is
   the shell, and the rules attach to the shell itself.

   ⚠️ **The class is still called `.admin-hero`** even though "hero" is the word
   being retired. Renaming it means touching the two dark-mode blankets in
   `style.css` that carry `:not(.admin-hero-note)` — the exclusion that keeps the
   subtitle white on the accent gradient, and which has already been broken once.
   The name is a scar; the risk of scrubbing it is not worth the tidiness. #}

{# ⚠️ **The title is the name of the menu entry**, read from `NavBuilder`, not
   passed in. `AdminNavCatalogueTest` already proves every entry has its key in
   all five catalogues, which is what made deleting the per-page `*.title` keys
   safe. `title` survives as an override for the four screens the menu cannot
   name: a single event's registrations, a package being edited, and the staff
   pass desk (which is not an admin-nav destination at all). #}
{% set _nav_title = nav_admin_title() %}
{% set _title = page_title|default('') ?: (_nav_title ? _nav_title|trans : '') %}

<main class="admin-page">
    <div class="admin-layout"{% if list_client_filter|default(false) %} data-controller="admin-list-filter"{% endif %}>
        {% include 'site/_admin_sidebar.html.twig' %}

        {# ⚠️ ONE grid item, holding the card. `.admin-layout` is `260px 1fr`, so
           two children would land in different columns — the table would wrap
           back under the sidebar. #}
        <div class="admin-column">

        {# ⚠️ "3 sur 11" the moment anything narrows the list. `11 machine(s)`
           beside a search box says nothing about whether the search looked past
           the rows on screen; the pair of numbers does. `is defined` rather than
           `|default` — `list_total: 0` is a real answer and `default` fires on
           empty. `?:` and not `|default` on `panel_note`: both fire on empty,
           which is what "not given" means here, but `?:` says so. #}
        {% set _count_label = (list_total is defined and list_count is defined and list_total > list_count)
            ? 'admin_list.count_of'|trans({'%count%': list_count, '%total%': list_total})
            : (panel_note|default('') ?: (list_count is defined ? 'admin_list.count_simple'|trans({'%count%': list_count}) : '')) %}

        {# ⚠️ **The search is captured, not written inline** — it is emitted
           inside the band, between the title block and the button, and capturing
           it keeps that one decision in one place. No block inside, so a
           `{% set %}` body is safe; `{% set %}` yields a `Twig\Markup`, so
           `{{ }}` does not re-escape it. #}
        {% set _list_search %}
            {% if list_search_placeholder|default('') and list_route|default('') %}
                <form class="admin-list-search" method="get" action="{{ path(list_route, list_route_params|default({})) }}" role="search"{% if list_client_filter|default(false) %} data-action="submit->admin-list-filter#search"{% endif %}>
                    {# ⚠️ `|filter`, not the inline `if` on a for tag — removed
                       in Twig 3. See `_admin_filters`. #}
                    {% for key, value in (list_query|default({}))|filter((value, key) => key not in ['q', 'page']) %}
                        <input type="hidden" name="{{ key }}" value="{{ value }}">
                    {% endfor %}
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m21 21-4.3-4.3"/></svg>
                    <label class="sr-only" for="admin-list-q">{{ 'common.search'|trans }}</label>
                    <input id="admin-list-q" type="search" name="q" value="{{ list_search|default('') }}" placeholder="{{ list_search_placeholder }}"{% if list_client_filter|default(false) %} data-admin-list-filter-search data-action="input->admin-list-filter#filter"{% endif %}>
                    <button class="sr-only" type="submit">{{ 'common.search'|trans }}</button>
                    {% if list_search|default('') %}<a class="admin-list-search-clear" href="{{ path(list_route, list_route_params|default({})) }}" title="{{ 'common.reset'|trans }}"><span aria-hidden="true">×</span><span class="sr-only">{{ 'common.reset'|trans }}</span></a>{% endif %}
                </form>
            {% endif %}
        {% endset %}

        {# ⚠️ `.admin-panel` **and** `.admin-list-card`. The first already owns the
           surface, the border, the radius, `overflow: hidden` (which clips the
           band's square corners to the card's) and the dark-mode `!important`
           block in `style.css` that a brand-new class would have missed. The
           second is what the band rules hang off, so they cannot reach the panels
           on the fifty admin pages that are not lists. #}
        <section class="admin-panel admin-list-card">

            {# **Band 1.** The workspace name, the count beneath it as a subtitle,
               then the search, then the one green named button.

               ⚠️ The order on the right is search THEN button, deliberately: the
               button is the last thing on the line, where it has been since
               S134h, and the search arriving to its left does not move it.

               ⚠️ **The one add button, and it is green (S134h).** It was
               `btn-primary-admin` — accent on accent, the same colour as the
               band it sits on, which is how the one thing a list page creates
               managed to be the least visible control on it. `--color-ok-fill`,
               not `--color-ok`: the semantic tones are *text* colours, and
               filling a button with `#86efac` gives a pastel slab carrying white
               text at 1.7:1. The operator saw exactly that on 2026-08-11. #}
            <header class="admin-hero">
                <div class="admin-hero-text">
                    <h1>{{ _title }}</h1>
                    {% if _count_label %}<p class="admin-hero-note">{{ _count_label }}</p>{% endif %}
                </div>
                {{ _list_search }}
                {% if action_label|default('') and action_route|default('') %}
                    <a class="admin-add" href="{{ path(action_route, action_params|default({})) }}">
                        <span class="admin-add-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>{{ action_label }}
                    </a>
                {% endif %}
                {# ⚠️ **This block was unreachable on ten pages until S141.** It
                   was only printed in the old full-bleed header, so every page
                   that had opted into `hero: 'compact'` silently dropped it —
                   `/admin/rfid-readers` lost its "pairing" dialog button that
                   way and nobody could open the pairing instructions. One band,
                   one hook. #}
                {% block header_extra %}{% endblock %}
            </header>

            {# ⚠️ The section still needs a heading in the document outline; the
               band took over the sighted rendering of it, not the outline. #}
            <h2 class="sr-only">{{ panel_title|default(_title) }}</h2>

            {# **Band 2.** One include, no conditions. Which of the three groups
               render — the tile row, "Affiner", the location dropdown — is
               decided inside the component, by what it was given. The
               `if show_venue_picker or show_tools` ladder that used to live here
               is what let a page lose its filters the moment a second location
               existed. The whole band disappears when it would be empty. #}
            {% if list_route|default('') %}
                {% include 'site/_admin_filters.html.twig' with {
                    list_route: list_route,
                    list_route_params: list_route_params|default({}),
                    list_query: list_query|default({}),
                    tiles: list_tiles|default([]),
                    tiles_label: list_tiles_label|default(''),
                    tiles_preserve_query: list_tiles_preserve_query|default(true),
                    refine: list_refine|default([]),
                    search: list_search|default(''),
                    venue_context: venue_context|default(null),
                    client_filter: list_client_filter|default(false),
                } only %}
            {% endif %}

            {# The active-filter chips share the filter band's ground: they are
               the state of the controls above them, not a third kind of control. #}
            {% set current_filter_chips = list_active_filters|default(workspace_filter_chips(app.request.query.all)) %}
            {% if current_filter_chips is not empty %}
                <div class="workspace-filter-chips" aria-label="{{ 'workspace.active_filters'|trans }}">
                    <span class="workspace-filter-chips-label">{{ 'workspace.active_filters'|trans }}</span>
                    {% for chip in current_filter_chips %}
                        <a class="workspace-filter-chip" href="{{ path(list_route, chip.remove_query|default({})) }}">
                            <span>{{ chip.label|default(chip.label_key|trans) }} : {{ chip.value|default('') }}</span><span aria-hidden="true">×</span><span class="sr-only">{{ 'workspace.remove_filter'|trans }}</span>
                        </a>
                    {% endfor %}
                    <a class="workspace-filter-reset" href="{{ path(list_route) }}">{{ 'workspace.clear_filters'|trans }}</a>
                </div>
            {% endif %}

            {# The escape hatch, for controls that are not facets at all —
               `/admin/reporting`'s date range, and nothing else today. ⚠️ It is a
               band inside the card, on the same ground as the filters: as a
               floating `.admin-panel` of its own it was the one thing left
               hovering above the card. #}
            {% if has_filters|default(false) %}
                <div class="admin-list-controls">
                    {% block filters %}{% endblock %}
                </div>
            {% endif %}

            {# **Band 3.** Emitted here, for every list, rather than left to the
               caller. `admin-flash` already carries the tone colours; a page
               writing its own is how one of them ended up with an inline
               hardcoded green. #}
            {% for message in app.flashes('success') %}<div class="admin-flash success">{{ message|flash_text }}</div>{% endfor %}
            {% for message in app.flashes('error') %}<div class="admin-flash error">{{ message|flash_text }}</div>{% endfor %}

            {# **Band 4.** #}
            {% block content %}{% endblock %}
            {% block panel_extra %}{% endblock %}
        </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    {% block after %}{% endblock %}
</main>

{# ⚠️ **The footer belongs to the shell, not to the caller.** S129 established
   that here, for the 25 pages on this list shell. S130b found the same split one
   level up — `base.html.twig` had no footer at all, so the 41 pages that do not
   come through this file ended in whitespace — and moved the include there, which
   is the only place that covers every page. This file no longer emits one;
   adding it back would render it twice. #}
